@startuml
title Launcher components and process authority
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "CURRENT interactive API - SPEC 0.5.0-draft" {
  actor "Operator / invoking caller" as operator
  component "curator umbrella\ncaller-side process" as umbrella
  component "curator env resolve --repair\ncaller-side subprocess\ncontext / home repair owner" as curator
  rectangle "curator-run process - invoking caller identity" {
    component "Config / trust reporting\nclosed fragment reader\nhost and permission selection" as config
    component "agents-management\nin-process Go library\nadmission / plan construction" as composer
    component "Provider-limit gate\nexplicit AvailabilityFor read" as limits
    component "Network selection\nin-process network / adapter libraries\noptional direct scope only" as network
    component "Composition / late checks\nno provider argv rebuilding" as compose
    component "Direct child executor\nwait / terminal restoration\nsignal forwarding, stop/continue" as executor
    component "ax document / hosted payload exporter" as exporter
  }
  component "Native provider child\ncaller-side identity" as child
  component "ax start subprocess\nprocess / terminal / session owner" as ax
  component "task-board session launch-plan\nprivate receiver subprocess\nterminal / deadlines / completion owner" as receiver
  database "Managed profile / home\npersistent: Curator owns\nlauncher never writes" as home
  database "Session Record\npersistent: ax owns" as record
  operator --> umbrella : curator run ...
  umbrella --> config : trust-root dispatch (SPEC 2)
  operator --> config : direct curator-run ...
  config --> curator : resolve canonical env-id
  curator --> home : resolve / repair
  curator --> config : closed v1/v2/v3 fragment
  config --> composer : LaunchModeInteractive request
  composer --> limits : admitted plan value, no process
  limits --> network : serviceable verdict only
  network --> compose : optional admitted patch
  compose --> executor : direct composed value
  executor --> child : starts and waits; no PTY
  compose --> exporter : destination contract
  exporter --> ax : launch-plan on stdin
  ax --> record : records Curator extensions
  exporter --> receiver : payload stdin + terminal FD3 / status FD4
  note right of config
    [[../SPEC.md#2-discovery-and-naming SPEC 2]]: trust roots belong to Curator;
    revision A warns, revision B refuses outside roots.
    Launcher reports its resolved executable path.
    [[../SPEC.md#47-the-launchers-configuration-file-family SPEC 4.7]]: config read failure is refusal, never absence.
  end note
  note bottom of compose
    [[../SPEC.md#4-composition-algorithm SPEC 4]] / [[../SPEC.md#6-errors-and-diagnostics SPEC 6]]:
    unsupported mode / mapping, permission, provider-limit,
    context collision, network or late-check failure is terminal.
    ax / hosted refusal never falls back to a direct child.
    Deliberate retry re-runs Curator repair; no automatic downgrade.
  end note
  note bottom of receiver
    Hosted Phase 1: Claude only, terminal stdin only (SPEC 4.8-4.9).
    Native paths do not probe a receiver.
    ax and hosted destination process UID / hosted durable-state layout:
    unspecified in spec 4.6 / 4.9; no launcher session state.
    Direct child status propagates; signal exit 128 + signal.
    [[../README.md#environment-and-transport README Environment and transport]].
  end note
}

package "TARGET one-shot - dispatcher v0 local headless; NOT IMPLEMENTED" {
  component "Caller process\nresolves / composes immutable plan" as caller
  component "swarma-dispatcher\nUnix-socket service from first slice\nrecovery / readiness before admission" as dispatcher
  component "swarma-user-launcher\nroot, no-argument sudo entry\napproved executor / generation checks" as privileged
  component "curator-run exec adapter\nworker-<label> / agent UID\nverify plan and binding; execute" as agent
  component "Shared launch library\nwith swarma-session-runner\npackage / API / release unpublished" as shared
  component "swarma-credential-broker\npeer-authenticated lease / renew\nsole rotating-account refresh owner" as broker
  component "Admitted harness\nagent-side process\nqualified credential channel" as harness
  component "swarma-user-manager helper\nroot; owned exec.stop" as helper
  component "Session host\nservice principal; closed delivery fence" as targethost
  component "swarma-session-runner\nagent-side approved executor" as targetrunner
  component "Workspace materialize / export\napproved executors under child UID\ndispatcher workspace contract (R-TRANSFER)" as workspaceexec
  component "Board change requests\norchestrator imports / exact C review / integrates" as changes
  dispatcher --> workspaceexec : materialize before work; export after confirmed absence
  workspaceexec --> dispatcher : change set only; no worker Git history / push
  dispatcher --> changes : result only to original caller; board accepts resource
  caller --> dispatcher : Unix-socket client; composed plan; authority / size gates
  targethost --> dispatcher : host_start / host_stop in dispatch-op/1; session-scoped host admission permit
  privileged --> targetrunner : approved agent-side runner
  targetrunner --> targethost : fresh authenticated channel; epoch registration / readiness before delivery
  targetrunner --> shared : required target library
  dispatcher --> privileged : only privileged start caller; admitted request on stdin
  privileged --> agent : user-manager descriptor lifecycle; read-only plan FD3
  agent --> shared : required target library
  agent --> broker : fresh connection after UID drop
  agent --> harness : verified plan; qualified material at execution
  dispatcher --> broker : owns bind / unbind effects (separate from executor lease)
  dispatcher --> helper : owned stop / account retirement; separate confirmed effects
  note right of agent
    [[../SPEC.md#10-agent-account-one-shot-exec-contract-target-amendment SPEC 10]] / [[../SPEC.md#102-caller-dispatcher-privileged-launcher-and-executor SPEC 10.2]]:
    No agent-side profile resolution, composition, defaults or self-admission.
    Broker via declared Unix socket; local trusted harness uses bound provider proxy only.
    First broker consumer: one protected Claude launch, Slice 0.
    Board runner / session host ask dispatcher; no embedded broker client.
    No interactive / remote / resume / seeded path in dispatcher v0.
  end note
  note bottom of dispatcher
    [[../SPEC.md#104-signals-stop-receipts-and-cleanup SPEC 10.4]]:
    Dispatcher owns claims, records, supervision and cleanup.
    Confirm absence before capacity release / replacement.
    One-shot identity revocation only after retirement;
    standing identities remain operator-only.
    After quiesce / declared-key cleanup and recorded export or operator waiver, delete home.
    R-TRANSFER workspace export recorded or operator-waived before home deletion.
    Separate retirement metadata export: service-generated closed schema only.
    Caller-owned 0-2 and read-only FD3 only; no service / broker / root handle.
    FD3 mechanism joint publication required (SPEC 10.1; user-manager spec 7 / launch figure).
    Host admission permit: one logical_session_id; session lifecycle authorisation member unpublished.
    Successor host_start requires authorisation and previous-claim absence; idempotent per (logical_session_id, op_id).
    Each physical start: (execution_id, controller_epoch, op_id) claim / fence / receipt interlock.
    Fence changes prevent stale start / reconcile; ambiguous calls resolve same effect / receipt, no second launch.
    host_stop: configured host principal, execution under permit, journaled E-stop / exec.stop / confirmed absence.
    Recorded as host-requested; distinct from owner cancel; no start authority.
    Single stop / retirement scope: user-manager spec 4.4 / 4.7; all UID processes / service domain / quiet absence.
    Process fate table: user-manager spec 7 (R-FATE); replaced-daemon writer fence; no live supervisor adoption.
    Cross-account workspace: standalone repository; private .git / common directory / refs / index / fresh config; no hooks.
    No inherited .git backlink / executable local config / credential helpers; copy / reflink preserves rule.
    Linked worktrees only within one account; optional shared objects immutable / read-only.
    R-TRANSFER owner: dispatcher workspace contract; board import / exact-commit review / integration.
    Transfer formats and shared-object provenance / access / retention remain open (SPEC 10.5).
    R-TIME: authenticated / operator-controlled installer time source; durable dispatcher / broker watermark.
    Expiry max(now, watermark); not_before min(now, watermark); no untrusted advance; operator reset.
    Expiry-driven home / binding destruction also requires boot-inclusive monotonic elapsed lifetime.
    Service unavailable / unready refuses; queue / events / long waits later on same transport.
    Dispatcher / broker service UID: unspecified in spec 10.2-10.3.
  end note
  note bottom of harness
    [[../SPEC.md#103-broker-binding-credential-delivery-and-rollout SPEC 10.3]] / [[../SPEC.md#105-typed-refusals-exit-status-and-activation-questions SPEC 10.5]]:
    Binding, grants, ledger, source conflicts or unqualified channel refuse.
    Claude expiry / auth failure: re-enroll and restart, no refresh/fallback.
    Exact post-exec evidence / renewal owner transport: unspecified in spec 10.4.
    Codex personal is later / qualification-dependent; Muse subscription reserved.
    SH2 host_start / permit qualification and helper signatures remain open.
  end note
}
note left of agent
  Wave-5 launch obligations - SPEC 10.1-10.2 / 10.6
  R-TRANSFER: plan digest covers B / manifest digest / write scope / exec-profile reference.
  R-NET-TOOL: read-only task resources covered by digest; bound provider proxy only.
  No web by default; plan disables provider-side search, invisible to network rules.
  Only operator-granted trusted-circle opt-in: qualified server search or platform Unix-socket web service.
  R-STANDING: verify settings / hooks / MCP / instructions by digest before exec, or root-owned surfaces.
  Drift refuses (code unpublished); repair is explicit re-materialization.
  R-EXEC: D-PATH protected light-check wrappers / fixed subcommands; no heavy entry points.
  User manager owns OS exec allowlist; R-VERIFY builds / tests / code execution on another machine.
  R-UNTRUSTED refused in Slice 0 / user-manager v0; workplace zero egress / donor-side loop.
  Admission: R-CEILINGS / R-WATCH / R-ALLSTOP / R-RANGE-DENY / R-SOCKETS / R-SHARED (SPEC 10.6).
  Exact plan / transfer / opt-in formats and qualification remain open; no implementation claimed.
end note
@enduml
